MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The self-drilling screw assortment fits naturally with my recent drill bits, rivets and bolts because it gives me another way to assemble sheet metal.",
    "The mounting magnets, wire-protection supplies and pegboards offer practical additions to my repair work: removable mounting, protected wire joints and accessible tool storage."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The grommet pliers and inspection camera repeat jobs covered by tools I already bought, without giving me a clear reason to add or replace anything.",
    "The decibel meter, test leads and printer filament require specific tasks or equipment needs I haven't shown. General workshop usefulness isn't enough for me to choose them now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying a measuring or inspection tool seems to have been taken as interest in other measuring devices, even when they solve unrelated problems.",
    "My interest in workshop supplies seems to have been stretched to include specialized electrical testing and 3D printing, despite little support for those needs in my recent purchases."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent fastening purchases make complementary assembly supplies appealing, while another complete tool for a job I already cover feels redundant.",
    "I distinguish broadly useful repair consumables from specialized equipment: tubing and connectors feel worth keeping on hand, while test leads need a more immediate purpose."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my fastening and repair interests but sometimes confused useful additions with duplicate tools or unrelated specialized needs."
}
